      <details key="appinfo" value="&#10;              &#10;  &lt;m:formal-name xmlns:m=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/metaschema/1.0&quot;&gt;System Identification&lt;/m:formal-name&gt;&#10;              &#10;  &lt;m:description xmlns:m=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/metaschema/1.0&quot;&gt;&#10;    A &#10;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://pages.nist.gov/OSCAL/concepts/identifier-use/#human-oriented&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/1.0&quot;&gt;human-oriented&lt;/a&gt;&#10;    , &#10;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://pages.nist.gov/OSCAL/concepts/identifier-use/#globally-unique&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/1.0&quot;&gt;globally unique&lt;/a&gt;&#10;     identifier with &#10;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://pages.nist.gov/OSCAL/concepts/identifier-use/#cross-instance&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/1.0&quot;&gt;cross-instance&lt;/a&gt;&#10;     scope that can be used to reference this system identification property elsewhere in &#10;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://pages.nist.gov/OSCAL/concepts/identifier-use/#scope&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/1.0&quot;&gt;this or other OSCAL instances&lt;/a&gt;&#10;    . When referencing an externally defined &#10;    &lt;code xmlns=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/1.0&quot;&gt;system identification&lt;/code&gt;&#10;    , the &#10;    &lt;code xmlns=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/1.0&quot;&gt;system identification&lt;/code&gt;&#10;     must be used in the context of the external / imported OSCAL instance (e.g., uri-reference). This string should be assigned &#10;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://pages.nist.gov/OSCAL/concepts/identifier-use/#consistency&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://csrc.nist.gov/ns/oscal/1.0&quot;&gt;per-subject&lt;/a&gt;&#10;    , which means it should be consistently used to identify the same system across revisions of the document.&#10;  &lt;/m:description&gt;&#10;           &#10;" />
